        title: 'Be Going To: Prior Intentions & Evidence-Based Predictions',
        structure: 'Subject + am/is/are + going to + [BASE VERB]',
        rule: 'Use "be going to" when a decision was made BEFORE speaking (I am going to visit Spain in July) or when there is obvious physical evidence right now (Look at those black clouds; it is going to rain). Negative: Subject + am/is/are + not + going to + [base verb]. Question: Are you going to study tonight?',
